  "query_preview": "..\n\nToday through Friday...\n\nThe best period for snow from our ongoing system will be tonight\nthrough Saturday morning as the cold front moves through. The\nheavy wrap around snow band that some high resolution models\nshowed impacting Southeast Montana has largely shifted to the\nsouth and east. Models are now indicating that impacts from this \nband are most likely to be in Northeast Wyoming and Northwest\nSouth Dakota, with lower precipitation potential than yesterday.\nLocations along the Wyoming border, such as Alzada, may still get\nclipped. \n\nThe atmospheric setup with this round of snow includes a moist \nDGZ, synoptic lift, and upslope into the mountains and foothills.\nSteep lapse rates are expected along the cold front meaning snow\namounts will likely differ greatly over small distances. Short\nbursts of intense snowfall will occur under the heaviest bands.\nLocations north of a line from Melstone to Ekalaka are expected to\nreceive little to no snow. Locations south and west of this line \ncan expect 1-3 inches of snow with the higher amounts occuring \nalong the Absaroka/Beartooth and Bighorn Mountain foothills.\nSnowfall amounts in the mountains could (50-80% chance) exceed 6 \ninches on northwest facing slopes. Chances for snowfall will begin\nto decrease from west to east throughout the day Saturday with \nprecipitation having moved into the Dakotas by 21Z.\n\nThe coldest temperatures of the fall will arrive Saturday through\nMonday as high pressure is advected into the region behind our \ncurrent weather system. High temperatures in the high 20s to 30s F\nand lows in the teens are expected. Sheridan County is expected \nto see some of the coldest temperatures with Sheridan having a \n50-80% chance of having a low temperature in the single digits \nSunday through Tuesday mornings. \n\nStarting Tuesday next week, upper level ridging is expected to\nreturn to the region bringing warmer temperatures and dry\nconditions. High temperatures are expected to be in the 40s F\nTuesday and Wednesday before potentially returning the 50s F by\nlate next week. Torgerson",
